# Airsup isolation

`/airsup` is a standalone slice. Keep it easy to delete.

## Put Airsup code only in
- `airsup/` (routes, views, db, sql, public, revert)
- the marked `AIRSUP-BEGIN` / `AIRSUP-END` blocks in `server/server.js`
- `"airsup/**"` in `vercel.json` includeFiles

## China companies (`/airsup/china`)

Manufacturer onboarding is a removable subslice. Code lives in `airsup/china/` only. Tables are `airsup_china_*` only — never `airsup_people`. Pitch: Western buyers find the factory inside AI (ChatGPT, Claude). Free for suppliers. Buyers pay. Success is domain verified + published so an Airsup user can actually interact — not signup alone. The public list of those live factories is `GET https://www.tademehl.com/airsup/live-companies.json` (a JSON array: `name`, `domain`, `category`, `live`, `activated_at`). Same data, wrapped: `/airsup/china/live.json` (alias `/airsup/china/api/live`). Appearance there means completed signup and a live factory ChatGPT can ask. Scheduled outreach workers must fetch that JSON (not scrape the HTML table, not rely only on Sheets/Gmail), match by domain, mark those suppliers live, use new names as social proof, skip signup asks, and reconcile stale sheet state. A 503 with `live: null` means the roster is unavailable — do not treat it as an empty list. Never use emojis in scheduler/outreach copy. Gmail for the confirm link reuses the existing `tademehl@gmail.com` send grant. Remove with `airsup/china/REVERT.md`. Do not put China company UI on other pages.

This is not a chatbot on the factory website. It is an AI-native supplier network:

1. Factory verifies a mailbox on its real domain and publishes capabilities. That becomes a hidden registry entry keyed by domain. Nothing needs to appear on their site.
2. A Western buyer uses the Airsup ChatGPT plugin (`find_people` / `send_message`). Discovery searches the verified registry (our database), not a live scrape of the factory website.
3. People Airsup stays ChatGPT-to-ChatGPT (Gmail wake). Factory endpoints do **not** get a ChatGPT worker. The company side is our OpenAI endpoint (`OPENAI_API_KEY`, `gpt-4o-mini`) speaking as the factory. It may only use published supplier fields, including scraped-then-confirmed facts plus interaction fields the website does not have (WeChat, sample lead they will stand behind, reply flexibility). Goal: make the company money — qualify the job and convert the buyer into a customer / usable RFQ. Private/internal data stays out unless the factory published it. If OpenAI is slow or missing, fall back to the published-fields template. Never fall through to the people wait-loop for a factory id.
4. `send_message` to a factory returns the factory reply in the **same** tool result (status `replied` + `reply`). Put the full transcript in `_meta.ui.panel.messages` so the widget paints every bubble immediately. Do not wait on `resources/read` to show the current turn. Back-and-forth until a qualified RFQ exists, then email the factory mailbox.

Supplier-facing story: “Make your company reachable from ChatGPT.” Domain in first — scrape the public site and pre-fill setup. Do not re-ask website facts. Ask WeChat / sample lead / flexibility, then domain verify and publish. Do not sell an AI employee or a website chatbot. The onboarding page shows a labeled simulation first, then a website preview, then domain verify. Never present a simulation as a real buyer or a real ChatGPT session.

## Do not
- Import `server/db/supabase.js`, diary routes, or admin routes from Airsup
- Add Airsup links, buttons, or data to other pages
- Put Airsup styles in `public/css/style.css` — use `airsup/public/` instead
- Share tables with the rest of the site — use `airsup_*` tables only
- Fake a Gmail login. Real Google OAuth only (`AIRSUP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `AIRSUP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET`)
- Hardcode Tade (or anyone) as a match. ChatGPT finds people with `find_people` on the Airsup MCP
- Hold listing answers out of the directory. Every onboarding question is listed
- Use Gmail as the conversation. Gmail is only a wake from `tademehl@gmail.com` with `[AIRSUP]`

## Live
MCP URL is always `https://www.tademehl.com/airsup/mcp`. Tools: `find_people`, `send_message`, `end_conversation`. Caller identity is plugin OAuth. `send_message.person_id` is the recipient. Wake mail is a separate `gmail.send` grant for `tademehl@gmail.com` using the existing Google callback `/airsup/auth/google/callback`.

ChatGPT conversation UI is a widget resource (`ui://widget/airsup-conversation-v15.html`). `send_message` advertises `openai/outputTemplate` so ChatGPT can mount the iframe **while the send is in flight** — the widget paints the outgoing bubble from `tool-input` / `tool-input-partial` immediately, then the reply on `tool-result`. Do not wait for the factory reply before showing the chat. `end_conversation` stays template-free. Continuation and in-widget `callTool` results (`conversation_id` or `openai/widgetSessionId`) omit the template and set `resultCanProduceWidget: false` so extra model turns do not open another card. Keep `openai/widgetAccessible` so the iframe can call `end_conversation`. The widget is transcript plus an End conversation control in the top-right corner — no in-widget send bar. The user continues in ChatGPT; reuse `conversation_id`. CSP and unique `openai/widgetDomain` live on the resource `_meta`, not in the locked tool JSON. Transcript, other party, and thread list go in tool-result `_meta.ui.panel` and the authenticated `airsup://conversations` resource. Do not add a fourth tool. Do not put extra fields in `structuredContent` (`_panel` is stripped before structuredContent). Tool `content` is a short pointer (conversation_id), never a JSON dump of the reply — the widget paints the transcript. The widget sizes to its content (never a 100% empty iframe). First paint uses `_meta.ui.panel` or, if the host only forwards `structuredContent`/`content`, synthesizes bubbles from `reply` + the outgoing `message`. `send_message` still blocks until the other AI replies (no poll tool). One click on End conversation must call `end_conversation` with the current conversation_id.

People vs companies share the plugin but **never share a wait loop**. `send_message` asks china first. A company id or `cn_` conversation must return in that same call (OpenAI endpoint or published-fields fallback). A people id waits for the other ChatGPT. If ChatGPT sends both `person_id` and `conversation_id`, an existing conversation_id wins. Company lookup/turn errors must not fall through to the people waiter. Widget tool results must not load every thread (N+1) just to paint the current transcript.

## Endpoint prompt (Gmail-woken ChatGPT)

The callee worker is instructed with the verbatim text in `airsup/prompts/endpoint-gmail-trigger.txt`. That is the ChatGPT Gmail-trigger **Instructions** block. Do not paraphrase it. `/airsup/prompt` copies that file, then adds the trigger filter: new mail from `tademehl@gmail.com` whose subject contains `[AIRSUP]`.

## Revert
```bash
node airsup/revert-airsup.js
```
See `airsup/REVERT.md`.
